pg_dump → new cluster pg_restore

kubectl exec -it pg-cluster-postgresql-0 -n demo -- bash

pg_dumpall -U postgres -f /tmp/full_dump.sql (dumps (exports) the entire PostgreSQL server into a SQL script file.)
pg_dump -U postgres -d mydb -Fc -f /tmp/mydb.dump

kubectl cp demo/pg-cluster-postgresql-0:/tmp/full_dump.sql ./full_dump.sql

Create a fresh cluster at the target major version

kubectl cp ./full_dump.sql demo/pg-cluster-v16-postgresql-0:/tmp/full_dump.sql

psql -U postgres -f /tmp/full_dump.sql
pg_restore -U postgres -d mydb -Fc /tmp/mydb.dump

